      "end_summary": "Fixed the bug where builtin functions (like `time.asctime`) could not be used as pytask tasks due to `inspect.getfile()` raising a `TypeError`.\n\n**Changes made to `src/_pytask/task_utils.py`:**\n1. Added import for `CollectionError` from `_pytask.exceptions`\n2. Wrapped `inspect.getfile(unwrapped)` in a try-except block to catch `TypeError`\n3. When a `TypeError` is caught, raise `CollectionError(\"Builtin functions cannot be wrapped\")`\n\n**Result:** \n- Builtin functions now produce a proper `CollectionError` with message \"Builtin functions cannot be wrapped\" instead of crashing with `TypeError: module, class, method, function, traceback, frame, or code object was expected, got builtin_function_or_method`\n- The existing test `tests/test_task.py::test_raise_error_with_builtin_function_as_task` passes\n- All 40 other tests in `tests/test_task.py` continue to pass",
